      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update python-3.12 to 3.12.13-r12 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-15308: the incremental html.parser.HTMLParser feed() rescanned the buffer on every call, so repeated unterminated markup declarations could exhaust CPU. Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/153030 (3.12 commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/785df8f743800661961528970f8598edcd291c14), first released in CPython 3.12.14; see https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-15308. Checked Lib/html/parser.py for the buffered feed() that the fix adds (_parse_threshold) in the python-3.12 package of every build published in the DHI Alpine 3.23 repository, 3.12.12-r0 to 3.12.16-r4, x86_64 and aarch64; both architectures agree. Builds before 3.12.13-r12 lack the fix; 3.12.13-r12 and every later build have it (from that build the file is identical to the upstream 3.12.14 file). The range ends at 3.12.13-r12."
    },
